1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,640
Welcome back everybody!

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,380
In our last lesson,

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,480
we learned two spelling rules.

4
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:07,900
We learned the floss rule,

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:10,120
where we double the last letter,

6
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:13,040
and we learned when to use C,

7
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:16,960
k and c-k for the /k/ sound.

8
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:19,980
You worked really hard on those,

9
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:23,200
and today we're going to learn something new.

10
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,240
Today we're learning about two pairs of

11
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,740
letters that come at the end of words.

12
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:30,560
NG

13
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,200
and NK.

14
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:35,200
Let's begin!

15
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,300
I want you to listen to this word very carefully.

16
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:40,940
Sing.

17
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:42,860
Now say it with me.

18
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:44,760
Sing.

19
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,140
Listen to the very end of that word.

20
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:49,620
Can you hear it?

21
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,440
That last part says,

22
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:53,020
hmmm.

23
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:55,520
Here's the important thing.

24
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:58,640
We write that sound with two letters.

25
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,860
N and G.

26
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:02,140
But when

27
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,480
they sit together at the end of a word,

28
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:08,760
they don't say n and g separately.

29
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:10,440
They join together

30
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,280
and make one sound.

31
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:13,940
Say it with me.

32
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:15,660
Hmm.

33
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,080
Did you feel that?

34
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,100
The back of your tongue lifts

35
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,480
up and touches the roof of your mouth.

36
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:24,440
Try it one more time.

37
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:26,580
/ng/.

38
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,380
Great job!

39
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,120
Now let's

40
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,720
read some words that end with NG.

41
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:34,340
Sing.

42
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,220
The child can sing a song.

43
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,040
Ring.

44
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,240
The bell goes ring.

45
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:42,920
King.

46
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,360
The king wears a crown.

47
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:47,180
Long.

48
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:50,020
That snake is very long.

49
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:51,700
Sung.

50
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,320
We have sung that song before.

51
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,020
Look at all five words.

52
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,400
Everyone ends with NG.

53
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,320
Now listen to the vowel in the middle.

54
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:06,100
Sing has a short I.

55
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,440
Long has a short O.

56
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:12,400
Sung has a short U.

57
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,580
Every one of those vowels is short.

58
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,560
So here's the rule.

59
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,390
When a word ends with NG,

60
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:23,720
the vowel before it is usually short.

61
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,320
You're doing really well.

62
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:30,040
Now we're going to change one letter.

63
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,660
Listen carefully to what happens.

64
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:34,280
Bank.

65
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:36,020
Say it with me.

66
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:37,420
Bank.

67
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,200
Listen to the end again.

68
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,620
Can you hear an extra sound?

69
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,720
There's a little /k/ at the end.

70
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,160
Bank.

71
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:50,260
We write that with NK.

72
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,140
They make the same

73
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:57,180
/ng/ sound but this time a /k/ joins on the end.

74
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:58,740
Say it with me.

75
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,260
Mmk.

76
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,380
Can you hear how your voice stops at the end?

77
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,240
That's the /k/ doing its job.

78
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:10,360
Now let's read some NK words.

79
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:12,020
Bank.

80
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,720
We keep our money in a bank.

81
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:16,200
Pink.

82
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,540
That flower is pink.

83
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:20,400
Sink.

84
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,380
We wash our hands in the sink.

85
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:25,040
Junk.

86
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,960
That box is full of junk.

87
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:29,820
Thank.

88
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,220
We say thank you when someone helps us.

89
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:35,430
Look at them together.

90
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:38,700
Everyone ends with NK.

91
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:41,160
Listen to the vowels again.

92
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,300
Bank has a short A.

93
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:46,780
Pink has a short I.

94
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,980
Junk has a short U.

95
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,600
Short vowels again, just like before.

96
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,420
Now here's the tricky part.

97
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,320
These two endings

98
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,920
sound almost the same.

99
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,440
There's only one difference.

100
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,600
A little /k/ sound at the end.

101
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,440
Listen carefully.

102
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,180
Ring.

103
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:11,320
Rink.

104
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,220
Ring.

105
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:14,440
Rink.

106
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:17,340
Only one thing changed.

107
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,880
The second word

108
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,700
has a /k/ at the end.

109
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,240
Let's try another pair.

110
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:24,800
Sing.

111
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,080
Sink.

112
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:27,920
And one more.

113
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:28,120
Bang.

114
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:30,860
Bank.

115
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:32,360
Now

116
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,420
it's your turn.

117
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,480
I'm going to say a word.

118
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:38,940
Listen for the /k/ sound at the end.

119
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:40,940
Thing.

120
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,200
Did you hear a /k/?

121
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:46,360
No.

122
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:49,640
So this word ends with NG.

123
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,140
Thing.

124
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,540
Now listen to this one.

125
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:54,940
Think.

126
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:59,360
This time there was a /k/ at the end.

127
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,540
So this word ends with NK.

128
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:04,080
Think.

129
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:05,900
Great listening.

130
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:09,080
Here's an easy way to remember.

131
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,680
Both endings come after a short vowel.

132
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,520
And both come at

133
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:15,720
the end of a word.

134
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,800
If you hear a /k/ at the end,

135
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,680
write NK.

136
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,980
If you don't hear a /k/,

137
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,820
write NG.

138
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,820
That's the whole rule.

139
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:31,100
Your ears do the work and your hand writes it down.

140
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:32,900
Let's remember

141
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,340
what we learned today.

142
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:39,520
The letters NG make one sound at the end of a word.

143
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,000
Hmm.

144
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,300
The letters

145
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:47,740
NK make that same sound with a /k/ added at the end.

146
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:49,260
Hmmk.

147
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,520
And both usually follow a short

148
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,220
vowel.

149
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:55,720
Fantastic work today.

150
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,720
Next time we'll finish level five.

151
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,860
We'll learn about the letter

152
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,360
X

153
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,480
which makes two sounds all by itself.

154
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:07,480
And the tricky letter W.

155
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:08,880
Don't miss it.

156
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,340
If you enjoyed this lesson,

157
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,140
please like this video and subscribe.

158
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:15,900
And practise these spelling

159
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,780
rules in the English learning app.

160
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:21,640
It's free on the Apple App Store and Google Play.

161
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,250
See you next time.
